<p>President Trump said Tuesday that Iran had told Washington it was in a &quot;state of collapse&quot; and wanted the United States to open the Strait of Hormuz as soon as possible. He did not say how Tehran conveyed the message, and there was no immediate Iranian comment. The statement followed Iran&#x27;s latest proposal to reopen the waterway if the United States lifts its naval blockade and the war ends, while deferring talks on Tehran&#x27;s nuclear program. Washington said it was reviewing the proposal. U.S. officials said Trump was dissatisfied because it did not address nuclear issues from the start. Secretary of State Marco Rubio said any agreement must prevent Iran from moving toward a nuclear weapon, and Iranian Foreign Minister Abbas Araghchi said in Russia that U.S. demands had blocked dialogue. Peace efforts have stalled nearly two months after the U.S.-Israeli offensive began on Feb. 28, with Iran&#x27;s restrictions on the Strait of Hormuz and the U.S. blockade of Iranian ports central to the dispute. A ceasefire has halted fighting between Iran, the United States and Israel, but talks on a permanent end to the conflict remain inconclusive.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/y_zpe26DryxUoe5oI9NgXgsrWFrricE6HS8XrsNWSeWGaa-j-qi42Y2ONMs47qlVMCbbrG-asylGSo6X0xwPu_utx4PJ4AUPUyU-Hl2BeUI2FVTUiVqwqS2NEmiYXTK80OxUkCssAyhsfXMrb2uNE2bod3OJOYqjVBCQqpfXdzsqQmiinRNjmjq1dER4CuK6IaPJi4I6KIw7AGzLIcCmfu92XKBkJTahlseLeXAKgkNw0K-yX7UF-mZSa_tiClrvOTWch3CtjmxaSJDD_A' alt='Vehicles drive past a billboard reading &quot;The Strait of Hormuz remains closed&quot; at Revolution Square in Tehran on April 28, 2026.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Mediation channel: Iran passed written messages to Washington through Pakistan, and Araghchi traveled between Islamabad, Oman and Russia while the latest proposal was under review.</li><li>Administration debate: The proposal triggered debate inside the Trump administration over which side had more leverage and which country could better withstand the economic strain from the strait&#x27;s closure.</li><li>Tehran&#x27;s leadership question: Reporting described divisions among Iranian leaders over what nuclear concessions, if any, to offer and who could shape talks.</li><li>Diplomatic clash: At a UN nuclear treaty review, the United States and Iran traded accusations over Tehran&#x27;s nuclear program and sanctions commitments.</li></ul><blockquote>We have to ensure that any deal that is made, any agreement that is made, is one that definitively prevents them from sprinting towards a nuclear weapon at any point - Marco Rubio</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>President Trump: Trump cast the blockade as leverage, saying pressure was pushing Tehran to seek a way to reopen critical waterways and that Iran could call if it wanted to talk. (<a href='https://www.allsides.com/news/2026-04-28-0700/middle-east-trump-says-iran-heading-toward-collapse-hopes-tehran-sorts-out-leadership'>AllSides</a>, <a href='https://energynow.com/2026/04/oil-up-as-us-iran-peace-talks-stall-again/'>EnergyNow</a>)</li><li>Iranian Foreign Minister Abbas Araghchi: Araghchi argued the United States had achieved none of its goals and was therefore asking for negotiations, while saying Iran was still considering the latest messages. (<a href='https://theweek.com/world-news/trump-weighs-iran-offer-war-nuclear-deal'>The Week</a>)</li><li>German Chancellor Friedrich Merz: Merz said the United States was being &quot;humiliated&quot; by Iran&#x27;s leadership as Washington sought to use the blockade as leverage. (<a href='https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2026/apr/28/middle-east-crisis-live-iran-us-israel-lebanon-hormuz-nuclear-oil-latest-news-updates'>The Guardian</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2026/apr/28/middle-east-crisis-live-iran-us-israel-lebanon-hormuz-nuclear-oil-latest-news-updates'>Middle East crisis live: Trump claims Iran wants US to open strait of H